'''3.''' Any place covered with an arch or a vault like an arch: as, to pass through the ''arch'' of a bridge.—'''4.''' Any curvature in the form of an arch: as, the ''arch'' of the aorta; the ''arch'' of an eyebrow, of the foot, of the heavens, etc.
{{smaller block|<poem>Whereon a sapphire throne, inlaid with pure
