{{right|''Milton'', P. L., vi. 759.}}}}
'''5.''' In ''mining'', a portion of a lode left standing, either as being too poor for profitable working or because it is needed to support the adjacent rock.—'''6.''' The roofing of the fire-chamber of a furnace, as a reverberatory or a glass-furnace; hence, sometimes, the fire-chamber itself.

